{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8447688, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.844771+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "### Part A \u2014 Direct Vulnerability Assessment (AURORA-Specific)"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.850668, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.850671+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| Category | Status | Finding |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8548093, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.854812+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "|---|---|---|"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8591294, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.859132+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Discovered services to map to CVEs** | NONE | Phase 2 found zero open ports, zero banners, zero IPs associated with AURORA. No services exist to map against CVEs. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.863139, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.863141+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Default credentials testing** | NOT APPLICABLE | No interfaces discovered. No web console, no SSH, no management portal to test credentials against. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8671415, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.867144+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **VSAT terminal security** | NOT APPLICABLE | AURORA is a 14m pleasure craft. Vessels under ~20m typically do not carry VSAT terminals \u2014 they operate on VHF radio and cellular data if needed. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.871157, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.871160+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Signal K server exposure** | NOT PRESENT | No Signal K instances within Estonia on ports 3000 or 3456. AURORA has no onboard server infrastructure. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8751402, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.875143+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **AIS transponder vulnerability** | **POSSIBLE (AIS spoofing)** | AIS transponders broadcast position data on VHF frequencies (161.975/162.025 MHz). These transmissions are unencrypted and unauthorised. The only credible attack vector against this vessel class. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8791227, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.879125+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **VHF radio compromise** | LOW PRACTICAL RISK | Modern VHF radios are not IP-connected on this vessel class. No remote exploit path. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8832018, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.883204+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Onboard crew/owner devices** | NOT ASSESSABLE | Personal laptops/phones carried aboard are outside the vessel's OT/IT scope. Owner cybersecurity hygiene unknown. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8871427, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.887145+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "### Finding 3.1: AIS Spoofing \u2014 Primary Attack Vector"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8911867, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.891189+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "**Credibility:** HIGHEST for this vessel class."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8952675, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.895270+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "AIS protocol (ITU-R M.1371) transmits position, speed, course, and identity data in plaintext on dedicated VHF frequencies. An attacker with an SDR (software-defined radio, e.g. HackRF, USRP, or RTL-SDR), a laptop, and open-source tools can:"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.8994539, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.899457+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "1. **Transmit false AIS messages** \u2014 broadcast AURORA's MMSI (276017550) with fabricated position/speed/course data, creating a ghost track"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.903466, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.903469+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "2. **Spoof identity** \u2014 send AIS Type 5 (static and voyage related) messages with altered vessel name, dimensions, or destination"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9076087, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.907612+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "3. **Hide actual position** \u2014 suppress or replace AURORA's real AIS broadcasts with a synthetic track showing the vessel elsewhere"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9124286, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.912431+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "**Equipment required:** HackRF One (~$300) + laptop + GNU Radio / AIS spoofer tool"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9167316, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.916734+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "**Detection difficulty:** MODERATE \u2014 AIS base stations and MarineTraffic systems can detect anomalous jumps"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.921042, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.921045+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "**Risk classification: MODERATE**"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9252856, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.925288+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "- Impact on vessel: **LOW** (does not affect onboard systems or navigation)"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9295285, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.929531+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "- Impact on tracking data: **MODERATE** (manipulates public and maritime authority vessel tracking)"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.93384, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.933843+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "- Countermeasure: Standard VHF AIS has no authentication. S-AIS (Satellite AIS) can cross-reference but same protocol weakness."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9380786, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.938082+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9419866, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.941989+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "### Part B \u2014 Reference Context: Known Maritime Equipment CVEs"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452499.9460928, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:54:59.946095+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "While no CVEs apply directly to AURORA (no discoverable equipment), the following reflects the current threat landscape for maritime systems."}
