{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.0932815, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.093284+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Internet-facing systems** | **LOW** | Zero discoverable IPs, ports, or services. No attack surface. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.0975275, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.097531+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **AIS spoofing** | **MODERATE** | AIS protocol has no authentication. Cheap SDR hardware can spoof vessel identity. However, this affects data integrity in tracking databases, not the vessel's own systems. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1018384, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.101841+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Signal K / VSAT / ECDIS compromise** | **NOT APPLICABLE** | Vessel does not carry these systems. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1058028, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.105806+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Default credential exploitation** | **NOT APPLICABLE** | No management interfaces exposed. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1109042, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.110907+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Supply chain / owner device risk** | **UNKNOWN** | Owner's personal electronics (phones, laptops, tablets) may connect onboard via cellular or Starlink (if equipped). These are outside the scope of internet scanning OSINT but represent the actual attack vector for a vessel this size. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1151023, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.115105+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "| **Overall cyber risk** | **LOW** | The vessel itself has minimal digital attack surface. The primary risk is AIS data integrity. For a pleasure craft of this size operating in Estonian coastal waters, the threat actor motivation is also LOW \u2014 these vessels are not strategic targets for maritime cyber attacks. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1189885, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.118991+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1232002, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.123203+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "### Part D \u2014 Recommendations"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1273785, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.127381+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "1. **AIS integrity monitoring** \u2014 If the owner values AIS tracking accuracy, use a multi-source cross-reference (MarineTraffic + VesselFinder + FleetMon) to detect anomalous position jumps >10 NM in under 1 minute."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1319623, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.131965+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "2. **Owner device hygiene** \u2014 Any smartphone or laptop connected via cellular while aboard becomes part of the extended attack surface. Standard personal cybersecurity measures apply (updates, VPN, no credential reuse)."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1361747, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.136178+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "3. **Periodic recheck** \u2014 Rescan Shodan quarterly. If the owner installs Starlink or any permanently-connected device in the future, the risk profile changes."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.1403322, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.140335+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "4. **No action needed** on VSAT, Signal K, ECDIS, or management interfaces \u2014 this vessel has none."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452500.144731, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:55:00.144734+00:00", "phase": 3, "line": "---"}
