{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2522457, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.252246+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **AIS Jamming** | Physical layer: VHF interference 161.975/162.025 MHz | **MODERATE** \u2014 jamming AIS frequencies obscures vessel track. Easy with $50 RTL-SDR + TX amplifier. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2552896, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.255290+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **GPS Spoofing** | TTP MITRE T1465 (GPS/GNSS Spoofing), CVE-2025 (GPS receiver firmware weaknesses) | **MODERATE** \u2014 AURORA's AIS position data derives from GPS. Spoofing GPS affects both navigation and AIS track. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2583187, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.258319+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **SignalK CVEs** | CVE-2025-68620 (9.1 CRITICAL), CVE-2025-68619 (7.2 HIGH), CVE-2025-68272 (7.5 HIGH) | **NOT APPLICABLE** \u2014 AURORA has no Signal K server (confirmed Phase 2) |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.261288, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.261289+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **VSAT Terminal Exploit** | SAILOR 900 default creds (admin/admin), 1,382 global instances | **NOT APPLICABLE** \u2014 14m pleasure craft does not carry VSAT |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2659442, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.265945+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **ECDIS/Bridge Compromise** | No applicable CVEs for this vessel class | **NOT APPLICABLE** \u2014 no ECDIS, IB, or bridge network on this vessel type |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2686508, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.268651+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2712727, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.271273+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "### Part D \u2014 Strategic Threat Assessment"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2738109, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.273812+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "#### Likely Attack Scenario: AIS Track Manipulation"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2761815, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.276182+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Element | Detail |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2796288, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.279629+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "|---------|--------|"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2831557, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.283156+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Threat actor** | (1) Opportunistic \u2014 curious hobbyist with SDR. (2) State-aligned \u2014 maritime domain awareness operations in Baltic. (3) Criminal \u2014 vessel tracking data manipulation for smuggling/fishing evasion. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.286381, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.286382+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Motivation** | Create ghost track, mask real position, generate confusion in vessel traffic systems |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2897196, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.289720+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Equipment** | HackRF One (~$300) or RTL-SDR (~$25) + laptop + GNU Radio + AIS spoofer software |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2927136, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.292714+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Execution** | Broadcast fake Type 1 (position report) and Type 5 (static data) messages on 161.975/162.025 MHz using AURORA's MMSI 276017550 |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2957537, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.295754+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Detection difficulty** | MODERATE \u2014 AIS base stations detect anomalous jumps (e.g., 5 nm in 60s). MarineTraffic/VesselFinder algorithms flag impossible tracks. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.2986815, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.298682+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Attribution difficulty** | HIGH \u2014 VHF transmissions are harder to geolocate than IP-based attacks |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3031511, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.303151+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "#### Less Likely Scenario: Physical Targeting via AIS Data"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3059194, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.305920+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Element | Detail |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3086138, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.308615+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "|---------|--------|"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3119195, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.311920+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Threat actor** | Organized crime or state actor tracking specific individuals (owner/operator) |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.315339, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.315340+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Method** | AIS data from MarineTraffic/VesselFinder used to track AURORA's real-world movements and port calls |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3190732, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.319074+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Risk** | **LOW** \u2014 pleasure craft AIS data is public. Owner privacy concern rather than vessel cyber risk. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.322466, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.322468+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Countermeasure** | AIS Class B transponders CAN be turned off when privacy is desired (legal in territorial waters for non-commercial vessels under 300 GT) |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3257055, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.325706+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "#### Highly Unlikely Scenario: OT/IT System Compromise"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3290741, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.329076+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Vector | Reason for Low Probability |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3328238, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.332826+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "|--------|---------------------------|"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3365176, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.336520+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Remote exploit | No internet-facing systems (confirmed Phase 2 \u2014 zero Shodan footprint) |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3403542, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.340357+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Physical access | Requires boarding \u2014 physical security is the owner's responsibility |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.344063, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.344065+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Supply chain | No networked OT equipment on this vessel class |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.34776, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.347762+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3512664, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.351268+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "### Part E \u2014 Recommended Detection & Monitoring"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3548682, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.354871+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| Priority | Recommendation | Tool/Integration |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.358614, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.358617+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "|----------|---------------|------------------|"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.362063, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.362066+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **P1** | Monitor AIS feeds for track anomalies on MMSI 276017550 \u2014 unexpected jumps, impossible speed, duplicate MMSI appearing at distant locations | MarineTraffic alerts, AISHub continuous monitoring |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3658607, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.365863+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **P2** | Set MarineTraffic \"port watch\" on AURORA's home port (assumed Estonian) \u2014 receive alerts for anomalous departure/arrival times | MarineTraffic (free account, vessel watchlist) |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.369527, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.369529+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **P3** | Occasional Shodan re-check (quarterly) \u2014 trivial given zero footprint but validates continued low exposure | `shodan search '276017550'` |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3735158, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.373519+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **P4** | If vessel carries cellular data (crew phones/tablets), monitor for C2 beacons via network analysis \u2014 this is the only internet path to the vessel | Not instrumented by default; recommended as owner-level awareness |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3818986, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.381902+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "#### M-SOC Integration Potential"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.386021, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.386024+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "For a pleasure craft, full M-SOC integration (Elasticsearch, MISP, Wazuh, Grafana) would be disproportionate. The only signal worth monitoring is AIS position anomalies \u2014 this feeds naturally into any maritime domain awareness system rather than a traditional SIEM."}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3938208, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.393823+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.3978434, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.397846+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "### Phase 4 \u2014 Risk Classification Summary"}
