{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4132898, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.413292+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Threat actor interest** | **LOW** | No known targeting of Estonian pleasure craft as a class by any documented threat actor |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.416946, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.416949+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Geopolitical exposure** | **MODERATE** | Baltic Sea ambient AIS interference zone. Vessel location in high-AIS-spoofing region raises the background threat level |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4207985, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.420800+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **AIS spoofing vulnerability** | **MODERATE** | Protocol weakness inherent to AIS \u2014 not AURORA-specific but affects it equally |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4249096, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.424912+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Physical tracking risk** | **LOW** | AIS data is public; any vessel in AIS coverage areas is exposed to this |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.428744, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.428747+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "| **Overall cyber threat risk** | **LOW-MODERATE** | The only credible attack vector is AIS track manipulation. No OT/IT compromise possible. Baltic geopolitical context elevates from LOW to LOW-MODERATE. |"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4322658, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.432268+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "---"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4356246, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.435626+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "### Recommendation"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4391875, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.439189+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "AURORA's cyber risk posture is **acceptable for a vessel of its class**. No remediation is required for OT/IT systems (there are none exposed). The recommended action for the owner/operator is:"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4432375, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.443240+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "1. **Privacy practice:** Disable AIS transponder when moored at private dock \u2014 this eliminates the only data leak (position tracking)"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4468849, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.446887+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "2. **GPS awareness:** Be aware that Baltic Sea GPS spoofing affects all vessels, not just commercial \u2014 have a paper chart backup for navigation"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4526453, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.452648+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "3. **Cellular device hygiene:** Any phone/tablet carried aboard should use a VPN when on marina or coastal cellular networks \u2014 this is the vessel's only IP-connected attack surface"}
{"event": "phase_output", "ts": 1781452670.4566913, "iso": "2026-06-14T15:57:50.456694+00:00", "phase": 4, "line": "End of Phase 4. Proceeding to Phase 5 (Analysis & Reporting) now?"}
